# KTrader — ignore policy
#
# Principle: source commits carry text that is part of the build, the test
# entry, the executable entry points, the release-bound credential chain, or
# the normative documentation. Everything else is local machine state and
# stays out of git.

# Market data, credentials, local machine state and generated release output.
data/
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.wanxiangshu/
dist/

# Archived development history: round logs, one-off scripts, research lines
# and delivery notes that left the active tree on 2026-10-10. Kept on disk for
# provenance and greppability; the authoritative copy of anything older is
# git history. This is NOT part of the release-bound credential chain under
# dev/evidence/{cpu20_acceptance,earlier_closure,final_2_0_0,release_freeze}_20261009
# (see RELEASE.toml and AGENTS.md tail). Only the convention README is tracked
# so a fresh clone still finds the archive map.
archive/*
!archive/README.md

# Local payloads. Fitted models, device executables and binaries are never
# text evidence; only their .toml descriptors and logs are tracked. The one
# deliberate exception is test/fixtures/t14294_conditioned_fold3.jls, which
# is already tracked and pinned by the frozen acceptance chain.
**/*.jls
**/*.jl2s
**/*.bin
**/*.so
**/*.o
hip_core_micro

# The one deliberate binary exception: pinned by the frozen acceptance chain.
!test/fixtures/t14294_conditioned_fold3.jls
